ha-citrine source patch 0004 against CitrineOS v2.1.0
(4fd7599b91c2fb6e6065e7c9b94be69880cced27), applied after 0001 to 0003:
OCPP 2.x charging limits from an EMS or other external actor.

Upstream v2.1.0 answers a station's NotifyChargingLimit and
ClearedChargingLimit with the empty response the schema defines and keeps
nothing: the limit, its source (EMS, SO, CSO, Other), isGridCritical,
isLocalGeneration (OCPP 2.1) and the schedule are found only in the raw
OCPPMessages row, so nothing can show which external limits are in force.

The patch adds:
- a ChargingLimits table (migration 20261026120000-create-charging-limits):
  tenantId, stationId, evseId, chargingLimitSource, isGridCritical,
  isLocalGeneration, chargingSchedule (JSONB), isActive, clearedAt, with an
  index on (tenantId, stationId, isActive);
- the ChargingLimit model, DTO and repository (Sequelize and Drizzle):
  NotifyChargingLimit deactivates the active limit with the same station,
  evseId and source and stores the new one, in one transaction;
  ClearedChargingLimit deactivates the active limits for that source,
  narrowed to the evseId when one is given;
- both request handlers store through the repository. A storage error is
  logged and the station still gets its empty response, never a CALLERROR;
- the Hasura table, tracked with its ChargingStation and Tenant relationships
  (role user, tenant filter);
- the OCPP 2.1 purposes 'PriorityCharging' and 'LocalGeneration' in the DTO
  ChargingProfilePurposeEnumSchema, so a stored 2.1 profile with either
  purpose validates (the generated OCPP models are unchanged), and tests.

The App's gateway reads the table read-only through Hasura (ha_reader,
/lab/charging-limits); nothing sends to the station from it.

